// Proposal 0179 Stage 8: a module function named after a class method wins
// over the generated dispatch stub, including from inside its own module.
//
// `Flow.Ord` is injected into every module and declares `compare`. Compiling
// it defines a polymorphic dispatch stub under that bare name — a global whose
// body panics. An unqualified `compare(a, b)` inside a module that defines its
// own `compare` resolved to that global instead of the sibling member, and the
// call panicked with `No instance of Ord.compare for the given type`.
//
// The sibling-member lookup existed, but the bare-name lookup ran first and
// there had been no global of that name to find before Stage 8.
//
// Expected: true false 0
import ModuleMemberShadowsStub.Version as V

fn main() {
    print(V.less(V.Ver(1), V.Ver(2)))
    print(V.less(V.Ver(2), V.Ver(1)))
    print(V.compare(V.Ver(1), V.Ver(1)))
}
